# Everything the image needs comes in as either a Docker build ARG
# (NEXT_PUBLIC_* — see Dockerfile) or a runtime env var injected by
# docker-compose (env_file/environment) — never as a file. Excluding every
# .env* file means .env.production.local (hosted Supabase credentials,
# see the memory of that exact gotcha) has NO path into the build context,
# let alone the image. There is nothing to accidentally COPY.
.env*
**/.env*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

node_modules
.next
.git

# Not read at runtime by the app itself — migrations are applied via the
# Supabase CLI against the database directly, not by this image.
supabase

# One-off scripts run manually with `node scripts/x.mjs`, not part of the
# running app.
scripts

docs
*.md
ADMIN_CREDENTIALS.local.md
*.credentials.local
.claude
.vercel
image.png
coverage
output
qa-evidence
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
